{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00465",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 3.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, am I early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.36,
      "end_seconds": 9.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Of course, put it down anywhere. So, how can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 13.18,
      "end_seconds": 16.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.82,
      "end_seconds": 19.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.39,
      "end_seconds": 24.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Yeah, it's heartburn. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.84,
      "end_seconds": 28.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.94,
      "end_seconds": 31.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Since yesterday, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.28,
      "end_seconds": 37.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.52,
      "end_seconds": 56.93,
      "duration_seconds": 18.41,
      "text": "It happens every other day. Maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Uh, and there's a lump feeling in the throat as well, two months now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.53,
      "end_seconds": 60.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.36,
      "end_seconds": 62.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.7,
      "end_seconds": 82.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any vomiting blood, anaemia, pain on exertion or black stools at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.49,
      "end_seconds": 87.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "No, no vomiting blood, anaemia, pain on exertion or black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.11,
      "end_seconds": 90.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "And weight loss, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.44,
      "end_seconds": 94.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "Not at all, no weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.66,
      "end_seconds": 97.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.73,
      "end_seconds": 100.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.37,
      "end_seconds": 102.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.45,
      "end_seconds": 111.97,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "I mean, just cataract surgery on my right eye, last year. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.15,
      "end_seconds": 118.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Okay, do you have any known allergies at all? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.53,
      "end_seconds": 126.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Pollen. I come out in... well, a runny nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.83,
      "end_seconds": 129.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.75,
      "end_seconds": 136.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.69,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.73,
      "end_seconds": 141.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Right, moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.08,
      "end_seconds": 143.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.59,
      "end_seconds": 145.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.61,
      "end_seconds": 148.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Asthma, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.34,
      "end_seconds": 160.29,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Okay, high blood pressure, that's already on your record. Good to know. Right, so that's your known asthma. We'll keep that in mind today. What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.26,
      "end_seconds": 175.1,
      "duration_seconds": 13.84,
      "text": "I take losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure. Seretide inhaler. I take it twice a day. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.08,
      "end_seconds": 179.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "So, how long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.46,
      "end_seconds": 183.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Two years now. Digene. I take it when it burns."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.87,
      "end_seconds": 199.36,
      "duration_seconds": 15.49,
      "text": "Mm. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.74,
      "end_seconds": 201.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.28,
      "end_seconds": 206.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.64,
      "end_seconds": 209.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Hold your arm out like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.3,
      "end_seconds": 224.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Tummy is soft and non-tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.17,
      "end_seconds": 246.84,
      "duration_seconds": 16.67,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.75,
      "end_seconds": 249.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.29,
      "end_seconds": 267.27,
      "duration_seconds": 16.98,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. This looks most like gastro-oesophageal reflux. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had heartburn, since yesterday, and no vomiting blood or pain on exertion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.61,
      "end_seconds": 270.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.49,
      "end_seconds": 277.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Let's get an upper endoscopy, for persistent reflux. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.4,
      "end_seconds": 282.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Sure, you know, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.62,
      "end_seconds": 296.17,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ECG for chest discomfort. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'd like you to take esomeprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, for eight weeks. It's for reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.37,
      "end_seconds": 298.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.79,
      "end_seconds": 321.59,
      "duration_seconds": 21.8,
      "text": "Smaller dinners, earlier in the evening, and prop up the head of the bed with a couple of extra pillows. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.53,
      "end_seconds": 323.23,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.81,
      "end_seconds": 325.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Come back in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.21,
      "end_seconds": 330.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.96,
      "end_seconds": 335.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.36,
      "end_seconds": 343.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "So, I take the esomeprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast and come back in six weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.59,
      "end_seconds": 349.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.91,
      "end_seconds": 354.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "No, uh, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.92,
      "end_seconds": 356.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}